AMEND THE RESTRICTED STREETS FOR COMMERCIAL VEHICLE TRAFFIC; TO REPEAL CONFLICTING ORDINANCES; TO FIX AN EFFECTIVE DATE; AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES.

THE COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF PERRY HEREBY ORDAINS that the Code of the City of Perry is amended as follows: 1. By amending Section 18-10. Through trucks restricted. of the Code of the City of Perry by deleting the section in its entirety and replacing it with the following: Any truck defined as a motor vehicle designed, used, or maintained primarily for the transportation of property with more than six (6) wheels shall not travel on the following streets or roads:

- (1) First Street from the intersection of First Street and Swift Street to the intersection of First

Street and Main Street;

- (2) Second Street from the intersection of Second Street and Swift Street to the intersection of

Second Street and Main Street;

- (3) Third Street from the intersection of Third Street and Swift Street to the intersection of Third

Street and Houston Lake Drive;

- (4) Houston Lake Drive from the intersection of Third Street and Houston Lake Drive to the intersection of Houston Lake Drive and Swift Street;

- (5) Northside Drive from the intersection of Northside Drive and Ball Street to the intersection of Northside Drive and Macon Road;

- (6) Carroll Street from the intersection of Carroll Street and Commerce Street to the intersection of Carroll Street and Macon Road;

- (7) Washington Street from the intersection of Washington Street and Main Street to the intersection of Washington Street and Duncan Avenue;

- (8) Jernigan Street from the intersection of Jernigan Street and Commerce Street to the intersection of Jernigan Street and Central Street; (9) Main Street from the intersection of Main Street and Carroll Street to the intersection of Main Street and Ball Street.

- 2. All ordinances or parts of ordinances in conflict with this ordinance are hereby repealed.

- 3. This Ordinance after adoption by the Council shall become effective immediately.

SO ENACTED this 20 day of October, 2026.
